// People. The crew members are made up for the example; their pre-flight levels are example
// numbers chosen by Claude. Tom and Elly are the names from the team's own example about personal
// norms (translated from the team's Russian: "Tom's resting heart rate is 70 on Earth and 60 in space;
// Elly's is 80 and 60"); their numbers are kept as that example and are not used for comparison yet
// (which norm to use is an open question). Ids carry no personal information: data files are named by id,
